From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Jul 2026 03:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH BlueZ] build: make bluetoothd-fix-permissions symlink-safe

On the EROS Q the rootfs is a read-only squashfs, so BlueZ's pairing state
dir (/var/lib/bluetooth) is baked into the image as an absolute symlink into
the writable /data UBIFS (Buildroot post-build). The install-data-hook then
runs `install -dm700 $(DESTDIR)$(statedir)`, which follows that symlink to the
host's /data/lib/bluetooth on any incremental bluez rebuild (the symlink is
already present from a prior build) and fails:

    install: cannot change permissions of '.../var/lib/bluetooth': No such file

A clean build is fine (bluez installs before post-build creates the symlink),
but every incremental rebuild aborts. Skip the state-dir creation when it is
already a symlink -- the post-build step owns it then.

Signed-off-by: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
---
 Makefile.am | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile.am b/Makefile.am
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 
 bluetoothd-fix-permissions:
 	install -dm755 $(DESTDIR)$(confdir)
-	install -dm700 $(DESTDIR)$(statedir)
+	test -L $(DESTDIR)$(statedir) || install -dm700 $(DESTDIR)$(statedir)
 
 if DATAFILES
 dbusdir = $(DBUS_CONFDIR)/dbus-1/system.d
